// Stalled (hung) JVM: the collector still delivers metrics, but every counter is frozen.
// A JVM stuck after back-to-back Full GCs keeps answering jstat with the same values:
// heap and Old usage do not move and no GC time accumulates.
// An idle JVM can also look frozen, so this requires high Old occupancy as well.
// Scope: dedicated Log Analytics workspace. Configure: measure = table rows,
// condition > 0, evaluation every 5 minutes, dimension = host. Tune the window
// (10 minutes) and the 90% cut-off to your collection interval and baseline.
JavaGc_CL
| where TimeGenerated > ago(10m)
| where record_type == "metric"
| summarize Samples = count(),
            DistinctHeapUsed = dcount(heap_used_mib),
            DistinctOldUsed = dcount(old_used_mib),
            GcMsInWindow = sum(gct_delta_ms),
            MaxOldPct = max(old_pct),
            LastMetric = max(TimeGenerated)
            by host, pid
| where Samples >= 5 and DistinctHeapUsed == 1 and DistinctOldUsed == 1 and GcMsInWindow == 0 and MaxOldPct >= 90
| project host, pid, Samples, MaxOldPct, LastMetric
